{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pulls/54","id":4594768665,"node_id":"PR_kwDORfqZes8AAAABEd6bGQ","html_url":"https://github.com/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pull/54","diff_url":"https://github.com/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pull/54.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pull/54.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/issues/54","number":54,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Keep Inspector outputs current and package standalone startup","user":{"login":"michaeljgrimm","id":12368053,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzY4MDUz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12368053?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm","html_url":"https://github.com/michaeljgrimm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaeljgrimm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Inspector output actions can read an earlier preview while a source or inline edit is current. Commit active public canvas drafts, capture the current raw buffer once, and use that snapshot for Copy, JSON/PPTX/PDF, Share and handoffs. Reject unsafe draft commits and suppress late output after source or navigation changes. Same-format JSON and Copy retain the accepted raw bytes.\n\nAutomatic share publication also guards the current source before and after encoding, and replaces a legacy import hash so a copied URL reloads the current document. Local production startup now uses the generated standalone server with packaged public/static assets, schemas and offline fonts; Vercel keeps its adapter build path.\n\nValidation on Node24.21.0: fresh frozen install, production build, TypeScript,692 unit tests and7 standalone controls pass. The final focused8/8 and full39/39 browser runs pass with zero retries; the full run took113.565407s. Four final screenshots were independently reviewed. Source review has no remaining concrete blocker. Fresh exact-head Linux/Windows CI is required before merge; no production acceptance is claimed for this head. Package versions and dependency lockfile are unchanged.\n\nThe first focused run was7/8: a held PDF401 response arrived after paste was initiated but before accepted editor input was established by the test. The final test first observes the new filename/title in Monaco, without another output action or deferred-preview wait, then releases the response. Product bytes did not change between those runs. The original trace and failure remain preserved. An old-head negative control independently reproduces Copy returning the prior title while the no-blur inline draft is active.\n\nThe original App54 head60c91f6 and first Windows result remain preserved: Linux31/31 passed, Windows30/31 failed during a31.4s Author navigation with a30.026s localhost asset delay. The startup correction does not establish that failure's cause or resolution. No retries or timeout increases are used to replace failed acceptance. PDF and Deckchat boundary tests use local mocks; CRLF paste normalization is recorded separately from exact action-byte preservation.\n\nPublic-app issue88 remains open. Native/font compatibility, the separate preset-history correction and geometry roadmap remain outside this app change.\n\n\nThe first additive commit57e5e59 failed both Linux and Windows type checks after692 unit and7 standalone controls passed: two archived test snapshots in the evidence folder still had `.ts` filenames and could not resolve their relative helper import. App builds/browser stages were skipped. The preview also reports module_not_found; its detailed compiler log was unavailable. The snapshots now retain exactly the same bytes as `.ts.txt` evidence, and corrected final-tree local TypeScript passes. Original first-attempt logs and metadata remain committed. Product source and browser assertions are unchanged; fresh checks on this correction remain required.\n","created_at":"2026-09-21T18:24:11Z","updated_at":"2026-09-21T19:39:40Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"551c523774877272cc58c86094da08519ebaade0","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pulls/54/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pulls/54/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/issues/54/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Data-Advantage/pptx-dev/statuses/6dfc2584698c1306505929a2bc3e427996d66563","head":{"label":"Data-Advantage:codex/inspector-share-guard-20260921","ref":"codex/inspector-share-guard-20260921","sha":"6dfc2584698c1306505929a2bc3e427996d66563","user":{"login":"Data-Advantage","id":104524841,"node_id":"O_kgDOBjrsKQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104524841?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Data-Advantage","html_url":"https://github.com/Data-Advantage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Data-Advantage/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Data-Advantage/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Data-Advantage/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.g